WEBVTT

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:02.742
Dominoes, quick starter.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:08.305
The First Flying Man, by Elspeth Roestron.

00:00:08.365 --> 00:00:16.039
Read by Ben Elliott, Wayne Forrester, Roger May, and Christopher Mills.

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:21.372
Published and Copyright Oxford University Press 2012.

00:00:21.432 --> 00:00:35.334
Chapter 1 A Young Man's Dream.

00:00:35.394 --> 00:00:47.926
My story begins in the 1630s.

00:00:47.986 --> 00:00:54.260
It is the time of the Ottoman Empire.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:02.984
Hazarafen Ahmed Chalebi is a clever young man of those days.

00:01:03.044 --> 00:01:17.752
He lives in the district of Ushkudar in Istanbul, Every morning, his arfan sits near the Bosphorus Strait.

00:01:17.812 --> 00:01:26.329
He looks at the tall tower in the district of Galota, across the water.

00:01:26.389 --> 00:01:33.775
The Galota Tower is taller than all the buildings near it.

00:01:33.835 --> 00:01:36.407
Simit!

00:01:36.466 --> 00:01:39.821
Would you like a simit?

00:01:39.881 --> 00:01:43.676
A man near his Alfen calls.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:49.550
He has some tasty Turkish bread rings on his head.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:54.384
But his Alfen doesn't answer.

00:01:54.444 --> 00:02:01.890
Every morning the man cries, would you like a simit?

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.814
But his Alfen never answers.

00:02:06.874 --> 00:02:11.638
He doesn't hear or see the man.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:14.939
He is dreaming.

00:02:14.999 --> 00:02:23.972
In his dream, he is flying over the boss for us with the seabirds.

00:02:24.032 --> 00:02:30.746
One day, I want to look down from the sky on Istanbul.

00:02:30.806 --> 00:02:37.452
He thinks, I want to fly across the strait with you, birds.

00:02:37.512 --> 00:02:57.755
But how?

00:02:57.815 --> 00:03:22.235
Weeks later, his arfen is near the Bosphorus again.

00:03:22.295 --> 00:03:28.906
Again, he is looking carefully up at the sea birds in the sky.

00:03:28.966 --> 00:03:35.597
These days, he is making some big wings in his workshop.

00:03:35.657 --> 00:03:39.558
He needs some help with the design.

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.583
His arfen!

00:03:41.643 --> 00:03:43.790
Someone calls.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:50.484
Esarfen sees his friend, Mehmed, with a second man.

00:03:50.544 --> 00:03:55.478
He goes over and says hello to the two of them.

00:03:55.538 --> 00:04:00.462
Esarfen, this is my brother Ali.

00:04:00.522 --> 00:04:06.990
Mehmed says, he's got some drawings for you from Italy.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:14.900
They're old drawings of birds' wings by Leonardo da Vinci.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.732
Ali says.

00:04:16.791 --> 00:04:18.884
Ah, yes.

00:04:18.943 --> 00:04:21.956
I know Leonardo's work.

00:04:22.015 --> 00:04:24.036
Hizarfen says.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.809
Let's see them then.

00:04:26.869 --> 00:04:31.262
Ali gives the drawings to Hizarfen.

00:04:31.322 --> 00:04:34.464
He looks at them for a minute.

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:36.625
Interesting.

00:04:36.685 --> 00:04:38.935
Hazarfen says.

00:04:38.995 --> 00:04:41.736
Then he gives them back.

00:04:41.796 --> 00:04:45.298
Thank you, Ali.

00:04:45.358 --> 00:04:51.502
Days later, in Hazarfen's workshop.

00:04:51.561 --> 00:04:54.973
My wings are ready.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:58.144
Hazarfen tells his friends.

00:04:58.204 --> 00:05:01.566
Let's see you fly then.

00:05:01.626 --> 00:05:03.366
Magnet cries.

00:05:03.426 --> 00:05:21.536
Your brother, Lagari wants to fly too, I...

00:05:21.596 --> 00:05:36.948
He falls.

00:05:37.008 --> 00:05:46.780
Mechmed hears a big crash and a cry from the foot of the hill.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:52.832
He goes quickly down the hill to his friend.

00:05:52.892 --> 00:05:58.392
His arfen is lying under his wings.

00:05:58.452 --> 00:06:01.832
Ali is next to him.

00:06:01.892 --> 00:06:04.652
His legs broken.

00:06:04.712 --> 00:06:06.992
Ali says.

00:06:07.052 --> 00:06:09.973
No, it isn't.

00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:12.854
His alphin answers.

00:06:12.914 --> 00:06:18.375
My wings are broken, but I'm okay.

00:06:18.435 --> 00:06:20.015
This time.

00:06:20.035 --> 00:06:23.106
Mehmed cries.

00:06:23.166 --> 00:06:26.317
But what about next time?

00:06:26.337 --> 00:06:29.968
Be careful, my friend.

00:06:30.028 --> 00:06:33.330
You don't want to die.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:41.076
They take the broken wings back to Hisarfen's workshop.

00:06:41.136 --> 00:06:43.598
Now what?

00:06:43.657 --> 00:06:47.370
Ali asks.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.862
I understand more.

00:06:49.922 --> 00:06:58.818
The design of my wings needs to be different, bigger and better.

00:06:58.878 --> 00:07:01.720
But that can wait.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.286
Hisarfen says.

00:07:04.346 --> 00:07:12.276
Right now, I must go and see the district chief of Galota.

00:07:12.335 --> 00:07:14.276
Galota?

00:07:14.336 --> 00:07:16.388
Mehmed cries.

00:07:16.448 --> 00:07:18.260
Why?

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:26.776
I want to fly from the Galota tower, so I need his permission for that.

00:07:26.835 --> 00:07:28.981
Forget it.

00:07:29.041 --> 00:07:36.040
The district chief never asks people into his office.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:40.494
Ali says, let's see.

00:07:40.554 --> 00:07:45.129
Hizalfan cries, come on.

00:07:45.188 --> 00:07:53.634
And he and his friends take a boat across the Bosporus.

00:07:53.694 --> 00:08:03.488
The three friends walk from the Bosphorus up to the Galota tower.

00:08:03.548 --> 00:08:09.722
Two tall guards stop them when they arrive.

00:08:09.782 --> 00:08:12.004
What do you want?

00:08:12.064 --> 00:08:14.166
One of them asks.

00:08:14.225 --> 00:08:19.640
We want to see the district chief of Galota.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.589
Hazarfen answers.

00:08:22.649 --> 00:08:26.729
Ali and Mehmed are afraid.

00:08:26.788 --> 00:08:29.219
What's your name?

00:08:29.279 --> 00:08:31.830
The god asks.

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:36.442
Hezarfen amed chilebi.

00:08:36.502 --> 00:08:46.156
Ah, the brother of the rocket maker, Lagari Hassan chilebi.

00:08:46.216 --> 00:08:50.747
All Istanbul is talking of him.

00:08:50.807 --> 00:08:53.198
The god says.

00:08:53.258 --> 00:08:59.240
Yes, his Alfen answers tiredly.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:04.282
So, can I see the district chief?

00:09:04.342 --> 00:09:07.032
He asks the man.

00:09:07.092 --> 00:09:08.713
Wait.

00:09:08.773 --> 00:09:11.284
The guard says.

00:09:11.344 --> 00:09:18.880
And he goes into the district chief's office.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:10:03.552
Chapter 4 A Brother's Help Sometime later, the guard takes Hezarfen to the district chief's office.

00:10:03.612 --> 00:10:09.546
Mehmed and Ali wait at the door.

00:10:09.606 --> 00:10:16.630
The district chief listens to Hezarfen's story.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:19.281
Very well.

00:10:19.342 --> 00:10:21.582
He smiles.

00:10:21.642 --> 00:10:25.883
You can fly from the tower.

00:10:25.943 --> 00:10:29.354
But be careful.

00:10:29.414 --> 00:10:33.976
Don't fall and die.

00:10:34.036 --> 00:10:37.837
No, District Chief.

00:10:37.897 --> 00:10:41.018
He's our Fen answers.

00:10:41.078 --> 00:10:45.900
And I'd like to see your brother.

00:10:45.959 --> 00:10:47.952
Tell him.

00:10:48.012 --> 00:10:51.066
Yes, district chief.

00:10:51.126 --> 00:10:55.378
Hazarfen says.

00:10:55.438 --> 00:10:59.550
I've got permission!

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:05.482
Hazarfen laughs when he comes out into the street.

00:11:05.542 --> 00:11:06.942
Good!

00:11:07.002 --> 00:11:09.714
Ali cries happily.

00:11:09.774 --> 00:11:11.774
What now?

00:11:11.834 --> 00:11:14.356
Mehmed asks.

00:11:14.416 --> 00:11:17.662
I must visit Lagari.

00:11:17.722 --> 00:11:21.378
Hazarfen says.

00:11:21.438 --> 00:11:27.992
So Hazarfen visits his older brother.

00:11:28.052 --> 00:11:36.066
Legari is working on his rocket when Hazarfen arrives.

00:11:36.126 --> 00:11:38.557
Nice design.

00:11:38.577 --> 00:11:42.018
Hazarfen says.

00:11:42.078 --> 00:11:43.619
Yes.

00:11:43.679 --> 00:11:45.780
Legari answers.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:53.204
Perhaps early next year, I can fly up into the sky in it.

00:11:53.264 --> 00:11:55.236
What about you?

00:11:55.296 --> 00:11:57.688
Me, brother.

00:11:57.748 --> 00:12:06.216
I want to fly across the sky with my wings later this year.

00:12:06.276 --> 00:12:10.720
So, it's a race.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:13.102
Lagari laughs.

00:12:13.162 --> 00:12:14.579
Yes.

00:12:14.639 --> 00:12:17.226
Hazarfen smiles.

00:12:17.286 --> 00:12:19.316
But listen!

00:12:19.376 --> 00:12:24.498
The district chief of Galota wants to see you.

00:12:24.558 --> 00:12:25.978
Right.

00:12:26.038 --> 00:12:29.579
Well, thank you for your visit.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.581
Good luck with your wings, Hazarfen.

00:12:33.641 --> 00:12:37.762
Good luck with your rocket, Lagari.

00:12:37.822 --> 00:12:42.578
And Hazarfen leaves.

00:12:42.637 --> 00:12:50.868
Two weeks later, Hazarfen's new wings are ready.

00:12:50.928 --> 00:12:56.674
Now I can fly from Galota to Uskudar.

00:12:56.733 --> 00:12:58.746
He cries.

00:12:58.805 --> 00:13:00.617
Wait!

00:13:00.677 --> 00:13:05.908
You must ask the Sultan's permission for that, I think.

00:13:05.968 --> 00:13:07.876
Mechmed says.

00:13:07.936 --> 00:13:15.338
And the Sultan says no to most people when they ask for things.

00:13:15.398 --> 00:13:18.669
So what can I do?

00:13:18.729 --> 00:13:21.660
His Arfen cries.

00:13:21.719 --> 00:13:33.044
Listen, these days the district chief of Galata talks about your brother a lot.

00:13:33.104 --> 00:13:39.068
Now, the Sultan's interested in him too.

00:13:39.128 --> 00:13:46.302
Perhaps, Lagari can ask the Sultan for a meeting.

00:13:46.362 --> 00:13:48.814
Ali says.

00:13:48.874 --> 00:13:55.916
So, his arfen goes and speaks to his brother again.

00:13:55.976 --> 00:14:00.698
Yes, I can ask the Sultan.

00:14:00.758 --> 00:14:02.908
Lagari smiles.

00:14:02.968 --> 00:14:07.209
But he can always say no to a meeting.

00:14:07.229 --> 00:14:32.298
Chapter 5 What does the Sultan say?

00:14:32.358 --> 00:14:56.600
So, legari speaks to the sultan, and the sultan says yes to a meeting.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:03.874
Seven days later, hezerfen goes to the palace.

00:15:03.934 --> 00:15:11.312
He walks past the higher Sophia, He is nervous.

00:15:11.372 --> 00:15:14.824
Please give me permission.

00:15:14.884 --> 00:15:17.174
He thinks.

00:15:17.234 --> 00:15:23.496
Near the blue mosque, he is more nervous.

00:15:23.556 --> 00:15:26.797
Please say yes.

00:15:26.857 --> 00:15:29.218
He thinks.

00:15:29.278 --> 00:15:34.454
Hazarfen stops near the palace.

00:15:34.514 --> 00:15:39.761
The Sultan can, of course, say no.

00:15:39.821 --> 00:15:45.952
Or worse, he can say, kill that man.

00:15:46.012 --> 00:15:48.462
He thinks.

00:15:48.522 --> 00:15:53.123
I'm Hazarfen Ahmed Chelebi.

00:15:53.183 --> 00:15:56.504
The Sultan wants to see me.

00:15:56.564 --> 00:15:59.874
He tells the palace guard.

00:15:59.935 --> 00:16:03.004
The man goes in.

00:16:03.064 --> 00:16:06.264
Hazarfen waits.

00:16:06.324 --> 00:16:10.678
He is very nervous now.

00:16:10.738 --> 00:16:16.362
After an hour, the guard comes back.

00:16:16.422 --> 00:16:17.912
Come with me.

00:16:17.932 --> 00:16:30.550
He says to Hazarfen, Hazarfen bows very nervously when he meets the Sultan.

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:33.306
Your Highness.

00:16:33.366 --> 00:16:38.312
I want to fly across the Bosporus."

00:16:38.372 --> 00:16:40.202
He says.

00:16:40.262 --> 00:16:43.864
The Sultan smiles.

00:16:43.924 --> 00:16:46.255
Ah, yes.

00:16:46.315 --> 00:16:51.126
Your Lagari has son's brother.

00:16:51.186 --> 00:16:53.308
He says.

00:16:53.368 --> 00:16:56.639
Yes, your Highness.

00:16:56.699 --> 00:16:59.650
His Arfen answers.

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:05.513
Then he asks for the sultan's permission.

00:17:05.573 --> 00:17:08.676
You have it.

00:17:08.736 --> 00:17:11.207
The sultan says.

00:17:11.267 --> 00:17:17.802
You must fly across the boss for us tomorrow.

00:17:17.862 --> 00:17:23.396
With a good wind, has our friend says.

00:17:23.456 --> 00:17:29.306
But without it, what then your highness?

00:17:29.366 --> 00:17:34.255
You must ask God for a wind.

00:17:34.315 --> 00:17:37.126
The Sultan smiles.

00:17:37.186 --> 00:17:39.918
Your highness.

00:17:39.978 --> 00:17:43.300
A vizier says quietly.

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:51.083
People can walk with their legs, but we don't have wings.

00:17:51.143 --> 00:17:57.386
Is a flying man good in God's eyes?

00:17:57.446 --> 00:17:59.728
Listen.

00:17:59.788 --> 00:18:02.380
the Sultan answers.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:10.776
We can think of new things with our brains, and our brains come from God.

00:18:10.836 --> 00:18:17.420
The first flying man must be an Ottoman, I say.

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:20.543
Yes, your highness.

00:18:20.603 --> 00:18:28.449
The vizier says, but he looks angrily at his alphin.

00:18:28.509 --> 00:18:34.394
that evening, his Arphin is not happy.

00:18:34.454 --> 00:18:49.261
There's no wind, he tells Mehmed and Ali.

00:18:49.321 --> 00:19:09.533
Hazarofen's reward.

00:19:09.593 --> 00:19:24.028
The next morning, there is lots of wind.

00:19:24.088 --> 00:19:33.245
Hazarfen stands happily with his wings at the top of the Galota tower.

00:19:33.305 --> 00:19:37.136
Suddenly, he jumps.

00:19:37.196 --> 00:19:40.088
He's falling!

00:19:40.148 --> 00:19:46.280
People cry, but he is not falling.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:49.450
He is flying.

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:57.433
with his big white wings over the houses of Galota.

00:19:57.494 --> 00:20:09.408
Hazarfen's friends, Mehmed and Ali, run with the people down the streets to the Bosphorus.

00:20:09.468 --> 00:20:15.490
Hazarfen flies out over the water.

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:19.078
I'm flying!

00:20:19.138 --> 00:20:25.268
He cries, people can fly.

00:20:25.328 --> 00:20:34.205
He lands across the strait in Ushkudah, a happy man.

00:20:34.265 --> 00:20:44.362
The next day, the Sultan has a meeting with his viziers at the palace.

00:20:44.422 --> 00:20:48.309
People can fly.

00:20:48.369 --> 00:20:51.446
He cries excitedly.

00:20:51.506 --> 00:20:57.912
And the first flying man is an Ottoman.

00:20:57.972 --> 00:21:02.366
That's good for our empire.

00:21:02.426 --> 00:21:07.450
His alphan needs a reward.

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:10.582
But your highness.

00:21:10.642 --> 00:21:14.070
The vizier nearest to him says.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:21.281
Lying men can land in our palaces and kill us.

00:21:21.341 --> 00:21:25.124
They're dangerous.

00:21:25.184 --> 00:21:30.758
The Sultan thinks about this.

00:21:30.818 --> 00:21:35.582
Yes, I see.

00:21:35.642 --> 00:21:39.345
Perhaps you're right.

00:21:39.405 --> 00:21:45.090
What must we do with his arfend then?

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:47.332
He asks.

00:21:47.392 --> 00:21:49.782
Kill him.

00:21:49.842 --> 00:21:52.904
The vizier answers.

00:21:52.964 --> 00:21:56.826
I can't do that.

00:21:56.886 --> 00:21:59.478
The Sultan cries.

00:21:59.538 --> 00:22:03.440
Then exile him.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:07.325
The vizier says.

00:22:07.385 --> 00:22:17.031
So the Sultan calls Hazarfen Akmed Chilebi to the palace.

00:22:17.091 --> 00:22:23.694
He gives a reward of a thousand gold coins to him.

00:22:23.754 --> 00:22:29.786
Then he exiles him to Algeria.

00:22:29.846 --> 00:22:38.148
Hazarfen says goodbye to his brother and his friends.

00:22:38.208 --> 00:22:43.358
He leaves Istanbul that evening.

00:22:43.418 --> 00:22:52.984
After that, he can fly over the Bosporus with the birds in his dreams.

00:22:53.044 --> 00:23:00.046
But he can never go back to Istanbul again.

00:23:00.106 --> 00:23:04.970
And what about Lagari and his rocket?

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:06.728
You ask.

00:23:06.788 --> 00:23:13.828
Well, perhaps one day I can tell you that story too.
